SOAPBOX: Mother Nature was working hard to keep me off 80 meters. Early in the week, a wind storm knocked down my neighbor's tree, which, of course, fell across my wire antenna.
SOAPBOX: Friday afternoon, the antenna was back up. On Saturday, a major winter snowstorm arrived. I measured 12 inches here. It was knocked down again.
SOAPBOX: Enjoyed Sunday afternoon here with some better band conditions. But no 80 meters.
SOAPBOX: Thanks to everyone.
